summary='''# R304 handback: 20 fixed records, credit 0

No complete source-qualified new ordinary endpoint survived. No CANDIDATE.md or Pi execution plan is warranted. Campaign remains 52/60 per the brief; this lane awards no credit and changes no shared metadata.

results.json contains exactly the twenty immutable reservation IDs, each with its entire literal statement, full parsed record, disposition, actual review depth and qualification limits. raw/ preserves each exact original line including its newline. literal-provenance.json records original chunk path, one-based line, chunk/raw/record/statement SHA-256 values. Reservation SHA-256 before and after is 1a0da14f7f616c16f0749d7cd80a6b60eb9079de613f6369f2784807b3d46ff3; all original raw lines and chunk hashes were rechecked at handback.

The strongest sustained mechanisms were 361271 (two-summand Laurent support allocation, infinite repeated minimum gaps and arbitrary prefix unpaid), 375393 (scalar-to-block Gram completion with dimension td unpaid), and 360957 (multi-mark primitive-factor insertion stability unpaid). ORDINARY_ATTEMPTS.md includes actual deductions, several attempted repairs, explicit failures, and precise missing lemmas. None is a formalization task.

Public/source exclusions: 364307 is the source's exact Theorem 6; 359387 is the source's Theorem 1.2; 373538 follows explicitly from the stronger source theorem using ker subset core and the cycle-count comparison; 360291 has an already public complete all-r construction. 364392 has a recent public complete proof claim whose main proof body was inspected, with external-dependency and journal-viewer limits disclosed. 375796 has a printed source counterexample in v3, with old-definition comparison incomplete. 359026 has an elementary omitted-normalization refutation. 359157 has a missing-coefficient discrepancy: at n=5 the literal sum is 64 while the public source enumeration is 70. These corrections receive zero credit.

History coverage is exactly the 262 allowlisted result files and authorized root ledger, STATUS, prior-context and upstream catalogue metadata (268 recorded reads/attempts total). Exact source-family matches were found for 2310.06464, on other assigned IDs; those distinctions are retained. Scanning is not semantic reading of every historical proof. No protected active crown lane was opened, scanned, hashed, globbed or polled. No historical evidence tree was copied.

Current registry heads were recovered from public HTML; pinned README/import/projects routing texts were retrieved and screened. Their absence of an obvious title match is NOT novelty clearance. The dated upstream pin was read. No GitHub API requests, access-control bypasses, browser/account actions, contacts, publication, git, child agents, Lean builds, solver/numerical searches or mathematical enumeration occurred.

Literature review is bounded and incomplete. Actual definitions and source proof bodies were inspected for the sustained routes; both Laurent arXiv versions and the typeset journal target were compared, and all three 1324 versions plus byte-identical journal download were checked. Not all versions of parked sources, relevant citing/companion proofs, journal corrections or figures were read. In particular no rendered figure audit was performed. No missing source or failed access was treated as clearance.

http-receipts.jsonl and source-read-inventory.json identify URLs, UTC, status/errors, bytes/hashes and depth. resource-and-process-log.json distinguishes actual local caps/measurements from managed-search limits and records quoting/parser failures, display truncation and the initial lack of a separate lane-local command log. The first TASK read used actual two-CPU affinity, timeout and CPU/AS limits, but its small CPU-selector awk command substitution ran before those limits; this is disclosed as a cap deviation. Later commands used fixed CPUs 24,25. All returned sessions and synchronous subprocess children finished; no jobs remain. MANIFEST.sha256 covers all lane artifacts except itself and its verification receipt.
'''
(L/'SUMMARY.md').write_text(summary)
manifest=[]
for p in sorted(L.rglob('*')):
 if p.is_file() and p.name not in ['MANIFEST.sha256','manifest-verification.json']:manifest.append((p.relative_to(L).as_posix(),H(p.read_bytes())))
(L/'MANIFEST.sha256').write_text(''.join(h+'  '+p+'\n' for p,h in manifest))
assert all(H((L/p).read_bytes())==h for p,h in manifest)
save('manifest-verification.json',{'utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'files':len(manifest),'all_hashes_rechecked':True,'manifest_sha256':H((L/'MANIFEST.sha256').read_bytes()),'excluded_self_referential_files':['MANIFEST.sha256','manifest-verification.json']})
print(json.dumps({'results':len(results),'credit':0,'manifest_files':len(manifest),'reservation_verified':True,'affinity':sorted(os.sched_getaffinity(0)),'peak_rss_kib':resource.getrusage(resource.RUSAGE_SELF).ru_maxrss}))
